# size 20x5
# A scrolling region whose top IS the top of the screen. The lines leaving it have left the screen,
# so they go to the scrollback.
#
# This case was written to assert the opposite - that a region never feeds history - and tmux said
# otherwise on the first recording. The rule is about where the region starts, not about whether it
# covers everything. See scrollregion-low for the other half.
\e[H\e[2Jkeep-a\r\nkeep-b\r\nkeep-c\r\nkeep-d
\e[1;3r\e[3;1Hrgn-1\r\nrgn-2\r\n
\e[r
